<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11147" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Corbĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Masc., a Roman surname</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hortensius Corbio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 3, 5, 4</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Fem., a town of the Æqui, in Italy</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				2, 39, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3,
				28, 10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A town of Spain, in the territory of the Suessetani,
				near the modern Berga</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 39,
				42, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>